            "description": "Watch Mirassol vs LDU de Quito highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 8, 2026. Tension was palpable under the lights as two determined sides met in a pivotal CONMEBOL Libertadores fixture. A Hard-Fought Battle On May 8, 2026 , Mirassol and LDU de Quito clashed in a high-stakes match where tactical discipline was matched by aggressive play. The first half was defined by heavy challenges and intense midfield battles, with Gian Allala receiving a yellow card as the match tightened up before the halftime whistle. Both sides struggled to find a clinical edge early on, keeping the supporters on the edge of their seats. The Second-Half Breakthrough Returning from the tunnel, the dynamic shifted immediately. Just two minutes into the second half, Lucas Oliveira broke the deadlock with a clinical strike that put Mirassol in the driver's seat. The momentum remained with the hosts as they pushed for more, eventually earning a penalty in the 61st minute which Reinaldo buried with composed confidence. Though LDU de Quito tried to claw their way back through late substitutions like Rodney Redes and Kevin Minda , the Mirassol defense held firm under pressure, including a late booking for Luis Segovia , ensuring the points remained home as the final whistle sounded."
